[size=4][b]PalSchema Hub — Community Schema Registry[/b][/size]

[b]On Palworld 1.0.3? Your mods are fine.[/b]
The whole 1.0.2 patch line (v1.0.2, v1.0.2.100993 "Mod Support Improvement", v1.0.2.101103) and 1.0.3 ("Balance Adjustments & Bug Fixes") changed [b]no[/b] DataTable row structs — every field that existed in 1.0 still exists, unchanged. That is verified, not assumed: the decompiled SDK's row-struct headers have not been regenerated since 1.0 (Source/Pal/Public @98ee60d, 11 Jul 2026). Check any mod yourself in one line:
[code]npx palschema-validate --migrate 1.0.2..1.0.3 my-mod/
-> no row-struct changes between 1.0.2 and 1.0.3 (both alias Palworld 1.0, SDK e663245)[/code]
[b]New in 1.7 — item mods get real value checks, ported from PalSchema 0.6.5.[/b]
PalSchema 0.6.5 (28 Aug 2026, its PR #145) rewrote the constraints in its own items authoring schema, and this registry's item-loader schema now carries them. The validator catches what it used to wave through: an IconTexture or VisualBlueprintClassSoft path whose asset name doesn't repeat after the dot (the report names both parts — the game resolves that typo to an empty icon), Rarity outside 0–4, negative Rank/Price/Weight/Durability, a new item missing a required field, and Weight/CorruptionFactor/Durability/SneakAttackRate/Recipe.WorkAmount written as bare integers where the loader wants float literals (1.0, not 1 — checked on the file's raw text, because a JSON parser can't tell the difference after parsing). $resource/YourMod/YourImage icon imports validate fine; they've worked since PalSchema 0.5.0.
[code]items/mymod.json > PSH_Sword /IconTexture: invalid value — ... (the path names "T_Icon_A" but after the dot it says "T_Icon_B" — they must match)[/code]
A field used on the wrong item class warns with the class that declares it (WazaID on a Weapon names UPalStaticConsumeItemData; the loader ignores it in game). Upstream's own schema can't catch that — its per-Type branches don't actually enforce scope, and its Weapon branch's "AttackPower" is a typo for AttackValue, which this registry scopes under the real name. Partial patches of existing items are untouched: the required list only applies when the entry carries a Type key, which the loader requires when adding and ignores when editing. MaxStackCount above 9999 warns too — the game duplicates items when moving stacks past it.

[b]Previously, in 1.6 — PalSchema 0.6.4 tracked, pal/item mod files validate directly, and a building reference.[/b]
PalSchema 0.6.4 lets new pals carry ranch suitability through a RanchActionData object in pals json (its PR #143). That key lives in PalSchema's loader, not on any game row struct, so the registry ships a loader-key overlay read off PalSchema's own loader source (RanchActionData, Loot, AbilitiesByLevel, IconAssetPath, Name, Recipe, Type, SortID and the rest), and the validator understands all three PalSchema file shapes: raw DT_* files, pals files ({"MyPal": {...}}) and items files ({"MyItem": {...}}). Target the release you actually run with --palschema-version. Warnings say whether the game would catch the same mistake: PalSchema 0.6.3+ warns about unknown item-loader properties at load time (its PR #138), but the pal loader silently drops unknown keys (its issue #134, still open) — so a typo'd pal field is caught by this validator and by nothing else. Also from 1.6: the [url=https://booyaka101.github.io/palschema-hub/buildings.html]building value reference[/url] — 460 buildings at Palworld 1.0.3, each spanning the two DataTables that share its row name, with materials mapped to item Codes and copy/paste row JSON.

[b]What is this?[/b]
A free, browsable database of every field you can touch in PalSchema raw-table mods — the answer to "where are all the game variable names?" ([url=https://github.com/Okaetsu/PalSchema/issues/53]PalSchema issue #53[/url]).

[list]
[*][b]Browse the schemas:[/b] [url=https://booyaka101.github.io/palschema-hub/]booyaka101.github.io/palschema-hub[/url] — 31 gameplay DataTables (DT_PalMonsterParameter, DT_ItemDataTable, DT_ItemRecipeDataTable, DT_BuildObjectDataTable, DT_PalDropItem, DT_WazaDataTable, ...) plus the item-loader schema, searchable, with every field name, type, example values and enum value lists.[/*]
[*][b]Item value reference:[/b] [url=https://booyaka101.github.io/palschema-hub/items.html]items.html[/url] — [b]2,445 current-game items (Palworld 1.0.3)[/b] with their ItemActorClass / ItemStaticClass / ItemDynamicClass, SortId, Rarity, Defense / Health / Durability and full row JSON to copy. Rarity variants are separate rows, as the game stores them (PlasticHelmet, PlasticHelmet_2 .. _5). (Cloning an armour row without ItemActorClass is why a custom helmet shows bare hair in-game.)[/*]
[*][b]Building value reference:[/b] [url=https://booyaka101.github.io/palschema-hub/buildings.html]buildings.html[/url] — [b]460 current-game buildings (Palworld 1.0.3)[/b]: Hp, Defense, DeteriorationDamage on the world-object side; TypeA/TypeB, Rank, SortId, BuildExpRate on the build side; materials mapped to item Codes; copy/paste row JSON for both tables.[/*]
[*][b]Version diff:[/b] [url=https://booyaka101.github.io/palschema-hub/diff.html]diff.html[/url] — what changed in the game's row structs between any two Palworld versions, now including 1.0.3.[/*]
[*][b]GitHub repo:[/b] [url=https://github.com/Booyaka101/palschema-hub]github.com/Booyaka101/palschema-hub[/url] (MIT)[/*]
[*][b]Validator CLI:[/b] checks your mod JSON against the registry and reports typed field errors (typo'd or renamed fields, wrong types) [i]before[/i] you launch the game. Raw-table, pals and items mod files all work, and --version now defaults to the newest known game version:
[code]npx palschema-validate my-mod/[/code]
[/*]
[/list]
[b]Did a game patch break your mod?[/b]
A Palworld update can add, remove or rename DataTable fields — and a mod setting a field the game no longer has just silently does nothing. This scans your mod against the real field-level delta between two versions:
[code]npx palschema-validate --migrate 0.7.2..1.0 my-mod/[/code]
It prints one line per affected field and exits 1 if anything broke, so it works in CI:
[code]my-mod.json > DT_PalMonsterParameter > ChickenPal000 > OverridePartnerSkillTextID: removed in 1.0 (was FName) — possible rename to OverridePartnerSkillNameTextID (medium confidence)[/code]
For the big one: across the 30 covered registry tables, Palworld 1.0 removed exactly [b]one[/b] field — OverridePartnerSkillTextID on PalCharacterParameterDatabaseRow (hitting both DT_PalMonsterParameter and DT_PalHumanParameter), replaced by the split pair OverridePartnerSkillNameTextID + OverridePartnerSkillDescTextID. It also added 23 fields you can now use, including EnemyWazaCoolTimeRate and BestWorkSuitability. Rename suggestions are a labelled heuristic, never a silent guess. 0.7.3, 1.0.1, the 1.0.2 line and 1.0.3 changed no row structs at all, and the tool says so rather than inventing a diff.

[b]How current is each part? (please read before trusting a value)[/b]
Field [b]names and types[/b] — the schemas, the version diffs, the --migrate scan — are verified against the [b]current[/b] game's row structs (PalworldModdingKit SDK headers @62fad41), and loader-implemented keys are read off PalSchema 0.6.5's own loader source (item value constraints ported from its bundled items.schema.json at the same tag). That part is 1.0.3-current, and it includes post-1.0 additions (InstallMaxNumInBaseCamp, CraftExpRate, drop item slots 6–10), renames (RedialIndex→SortId, HP→Hp), both array patch forms ([...] replaces, {"Action": "Clear", "Items": [...]} clears/appends) and $Filters wildcard metadata. Proven against real published PalSchema mods.
Row [b]values[/b] in the item and building references are [b]current too, scraped for 1.0.3[/b]. They come from paldb.cc, which tracks the live build (its footer pins to v1.0.3, 12 Aug 2026): [b]2,445 item rows[/b] and [b]460 building rows[/b]. Items added since 1.0 are present — Hexolite Helmet (internal Code SFHelmet, SortId 1325) among them — and the dead field [b]SortID[/b], which the current game renamed to SortId, is gone. Fields paldb.cc does not render (VisualBlueprintClassSoft and friends on items; BlueprintClassName, RequiredBuildWorkAmount and the raw Material columns on buildings) are filled from the Jan-2024 dump where possible or honestly absent. Gates in CI validate every row against the schemas and fail the build if the data ever goes stale again.

[b]What the download contains:[/b] a complete offline copy of the registry — all the JSON Schemas plus the loader-key overlay, the machine-readable index, the searchable browser page, the item and building value references, the version-diff viewer with all 12 version snapshots and every pairwise diff, and the validator CLI (MIT). Look up any field in a text editor with no tools at all, or validate and migration-scan your mod fully offline (the migration scan needs no npm install at all). The links above always carry the latest version. No game assets are included.

Credits: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/palworld/mods/2361]PalSchema[/url] by Okaetsu. Data derived via public community dumps (blaynem/paldex) and the PalworldModdingKit SDK headers (localcc).
